Spec: Database

Purpose:
  Drift schema mirroring the original Room schema, plus the ride summary and follow-link columns added since.

Owns:
  ./tables.dart
  ./app_database.dart
  ./app_database.g.dart
  ./database_connection.dart
  ./ride_dao.dart
  ./ride_dao.g.dart
  ./trackpoint_dao.dart
  ./trackpoint_dao.g.dart
  ./ride_with_trackpoints.dart
  ./followed_route.dart
  /test/data/rides_dao_test.dart
  /test/data/trackpoints_dao_test.dart
  /test/data/ride_with_trackpoints_test.dart
  /test/data/ride_range_query_test.dart
  /test/data/followed_rides_dao_test.dart
  /test/data/elevation_schema_test.dart

References:
  /docs/specs/history/03-data-layer.md
  /docs/specs/history/20-followed-rides.md
  /docs/decisions/0002-elevation-from-gps.md
  /docs/decisions/0001-ride-outlines.md

Must:
  Tables are `rides` (@Ride), `trackpoints` (@Trackpoint) and `ride_outlines`; trackpoints are deleted with their ride
    (`ON DELETE CASCADE`) and foreign keys are switched on before the database opens.
  `rides.followed_ride_id` is cleared when the original is deleted (`ON DELETE SET NULL`).
  `trackpoints.altitude` is the recorded altitude in metres or none. `rides.ascent_m` and `rides.descent_m`
    are the totals stored at save, or none for a ride without altitude data; older rides stay none.
  `ride_outlines` holds one row per ride: encoded polyline and bounding box; it is deleted with its ride
    (`ON DELETE CASCADE`, single and batch delete, each in one transaction) and kept when the ride is edited.
  The schema version is `7`; every older version upgrades in place without losing rides.
  Every schema change raises the version and adds an upgrade step.
  Reads are reactive Drift streams; @RideWithTrackpoints is assembled in the DAO.
  Generated files come from `dart run build_runner build`.

Must not:
  Edit generated `.g.dart` files by hand.

Done when:
  DAO tests run against an in-memory database (`NativeDatabase.memory()`).
